Design the backend models and services for a live cricket scoring application.
The system needs to track the state of a cricket match ball-by-ball, update the scorecard in real-time, and serve this data to front-end clients.

Core Requirements:
Match Tracking: The system must model a cricket match involving two teams, a specific format (e.g., T20, ODI), and track the current state of the match
 (Scheduled, In Progress, Completed, Abandoned).
Ball-by-Ball Granularity: Track every ball bowled in an over. A ball can result in normal runs, extras (Wide, No-Ball, Leg-Bye),
and wickets (Bowled, Caught, Run Out, etc.).
Dynamic Scorecard: Maintain a live scorecard that instantly reflects:
Total team score and wickets.
Current Run Rate (CRR).
The current striker and non-striker with their individual scores.
The current bowler's figures (Overs, Maidens, Runs, Wickets).
Real-Time Updates : The system must push live score updates and ball-by-ball commentary to subscribed clients or
dashboards whenever a ball is bowled, without the client needing to constantly poll the database.

Entity:

Match: class
Id, MatchFormat, TeamA, TeamB, MatchStatus, Scorecard, Time, Place, List<Innings>

Inning: class
TeamBat, TeamBowl, List<Over> overs, totalRun, totalWickets

MatchFormat: Enum
T20, ODI, TEST

MatchStatus: Enum
Scheduled, In Progress, Completed, Abandoned

Ball: class
BallType ballType, Integer score, Player bowledBy, Integer ballNumber, Player facedBy, RunType runType, Wicket wicket, boolean isValidBall

Wicket: class
Player dismissed, Player dismissedBy, WicketType type, Player caughtBy

Over: class
List<Ball> balls, Integer overNumber

BallType: Enum
Wide, No-Ball, Leg-Bye, Normal

WicketType: Enum
Bowled, Caught, Run-Out, LBW, Stump, RetiredHurt

RunType: Enum
Bye, LegBye, overthrow, no-ball, wide, normal

ScoreCard: class
Player striker, Player non-striker, Map<String, BattingStats> battingStats, Map<String, BowlStats> bowlingStats, Map<String, Ball> wicketFallen

BattingStats: class
Integer score, Integer fours, Integer sixes, Integer bowlFaced, boolean isDismissed, String dismissedBy

BowlStats: class
Integer Overs, Integer Maidens, Integer Runs, Integer Wickets

Team: class
List<Player> players, String teamId, String teamName

Player: class
String playerId, String playerName, PlayerRole role

PlayerRole: Enum
Batsman, Bowler, All-rounder, wicket-keeper

Subject: interface
addObserver(ScoreObserver), removeObserver(ScoreObserver), notifyObserver()

CommentaryService: class implements Subject
recordBall(Ball ball) {notifyObserver()}

ScoreObserver: interface
updateScore(Match match, ScoreCard scoreCard)